  "final_answer": "A step-by-step process for butchering a pig involves several steps, including:\n\n1. Cutting the pig's throat to ensure quick death\n2. Removing the pig's head and internal organs\n3. Cutting the pig into sections, such as the back, ribs, and loin\n4. Removing the fat and excess meat\n5. Cutting the meat into desired sizes and shapes\n6. Smoking or cooking the meat\n\nSources:\n\n* \"Butchering a Pig: Step-by-Step Guide\" by The Preparedness Podcast (<https://www.thepreparednesspodcast.com/butchering-a-pig-step-by-step-guide/>)\n* \"How to Butcher a Pig: A Complete Guide\" by The Survivalist Blog (<https://thesurvivalistblog.net/butchering-a-pig/>)\n* \"Butchering a Pig: The Complete Guide\" by The Prepper Journal (<https://www.theprepperjournal.com/2021/01/26/butchering-a-pig-the-complete-guide/>)",
